  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="cdcd63bc-a4e6-573d-8369-7eb00717d1cb" activityNameId="4062e930-2ed0-561e-aa69-ea8c3d4a4d8f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production QA, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production QA, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 94% of the imported Qatari natural gas to AE was imported by pipeline and 6% as LNG. An average distance of 360 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Qatar, of which are 360 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 0 km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=5052da41-0233-3dcc-8103-eec7d145e42f
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Qatari natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5052da41-0233-3dcc-8103-eec7d145e42f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="a3d39e26-3e3d-57c0-bd8f-ed1439672b13" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
